.TH HD-BOOTLOADER-UPDATE 8 "October 2026" "hd-bootloader" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-bootloader-update \- write the hyprdebian bootloader and its UKIs to an EFI system partition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-bootloader-update
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-bootloader-update
reads the settings from the key
.B hd-bootloader
in
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
and writes, below the EFI system partition given with
.B \-\-esp
.RI ( /boot/efi
by default):
.TP
.I EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
the bootloader of the frontend of the installed package;
.TP
.I EFI/BOOT/assets.efi
the settings, the menu rows, the DKMS MOK and the assets of the frontend,
as sections of a PE image that the bootloader loads with LoadImage, so the
firmware checks its signature under Secure Boot;
.TP
.I EFI/Linux/HyprDebian\-Kernel\-x.y.z.efi
multi-profile UKIs of the four most recent kernels in
.IR /boot ,
with a normal and a ZFS recovery profile.
.PP
See
.BR hd-bootloader (7)
for the settings.
Usually it is not run by hand, but by
.I /usr/lib/hd-bootloader/update-esps
for every ESP.
.PP
The files are written in an order that leaves a bootable ESP when it is
interrupted: first the UKIs, then
.I assets.efi
and
.IR BOOTX64.EFI ,
and only then are the UKIs of older kernels removed.
A file whose contents would not change is not rewritten.
.PP
When the Secure Boot keys of
.BR hd-secboot (7)
are in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/secboot ,
the files are signed with the db key before they replace those on the ESP;
a file that would not change is signed again when it does not verify with
the db certificate.
Without the keys, the files are written unsigned, with a message saying so.
The message of each file written says whether it is signed or unsigned.
.PP
Run it as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-esp " dir"
The root of the EFI system partition to write to;
.I /boot/efi
by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read the settings from the JSON object in
.I file
instead of the key
.B hd-bootloader
in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-boot\-dir " dir"
Where the kernels are;
.I /boot
by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-mok " file"
The certificate of the DKMS MOK, DER or PEM;
.I /var/lib/dkms/mok.pub
by default.
It is needed to boot with the ZFS module.
.TP
.BI \-\-db\-key " file"
.TQ
.BI \-\-db\-cert " file"
The Secure Boot db key and its PEM certificate;
.I /etc/hyprdebian/secboot/db.key
and
.I db.crt
by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-bootloader\-dir " dir"
.TQ
.BI \-\-assets\-stub " file"
Where the compiled bootloaders and the assets stub are;
.I /usr/lib/hd-bootloader
by default.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the ESP was written, not 0 on an error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Update the ESP in
.IR /boot/efi :
.PP
.RS
hd-bootloader-update
.RE
.PP
Update the ESP in
.IR /boot/efi2 :
.PP
.RS
hd-bootloader-update \-\-esp /boot/efi2
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-bootloader (7),
.BR hd-secboot (7),
.BR ukify (1),
.BR sbsign (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
